1
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:05,839
Chapter 4. the counterpay.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:10,718
Upon waking next morning about daylight, I found Qui Quag's arm thrown over me in

3
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:13,278
the most loving and affectionate manner.

4
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:17,599
He had almost thought I had been his wife. The counterpane was of patchwork

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:22,559
full of odd little partycoled squares and triangles, and this arm of his

6
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:28,078
tattooed all over with an interminable labyrinth of a figure, no two

7
00:00:28,079 --> 00:00:32,638
parts of which were of one precise shade, owing, I suppose, to his keeping

8
00:00:32,639 --> 00:00:37,678
his arm at sea unmethodically in sun and shade, his shirt sleeves irregularly

9
00:00:37,679 --> 00:00:42,478
rolled up at various times. This same arm of his, I say, looked for all the

10
00:00:42,479 --> 00:00:47,599
world like a strip of that same patchwork quilt. Indeed, partly lying on

11
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:51,919
it as the arm did when I first awoke, I could hardly tell it from the quilt they

12
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:56,157
so blended their hues together, and it was only by the sense of weight and

13
00:00:56,158 --> 00:01:01,038
pressure that I could tell that Quiquake was hugging me. My sensations were

14
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:04,718
strange. Let me try to explain them.

15
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:08,799
When I was a child, I well remember a somewhat similar circumstance that

16
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,478
befell me. Whether it was a reality or a dream, I never could entirely settle.

17
00:01:14,479 --> 00:01:19,599
The circumstance was this. I had been cutting up some caper or other. I think

18
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:24,078
it was trying to crawl up the chimney, as I had seen a little sweep do a few

19
00:01:24,079 --> 00:01:28,718
days previous, and my stepmother, who somehow or other was all the time

20
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:33,197
whipping me or sending me to bed supperless, my mother dragged me by the

21
00:01:33,198 --> 00:01:37,519
legs out of the chimney and packed me off to bed, though it was only 2:00 in

22
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:41,919
the afternoon of the 21st June, the longest day of the year in our

23
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:47,919
hemisphere. I felt dreadfully, but there was no help for it. So upstairs I went

24
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:52,799
to my little room in the third floor, undressed myself as slowly as possible

25
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:58,318
so as to kill time, and with a bitter sigh, got between the sheets. I lay

26
00:01:58,319 --> 00:02:03,197
there dismally calculating that 16 entire hours must elapse before I could

27
00:02:03,198 --> 00:02:05,358
hope for a resurrection.

28
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:11,038
16 hours in bed. The small of my back achd to think of it, and it was so

29
00:02:11,039 --> 00:02:15,438
light, too, the sun shining in at the window, and a great rattling of coaches

30
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:20,638
in the streets, and the sound of gay voices all over the house. I felt worse

31
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:25,999
and worse. At last I got up, dressed, and softly going down in my stocking

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,478
feet, sought out my stepmother, and suddenly threw myself at her feet,

33
00:02:30,479 --> 00:02:34,638
beseeching her as a particular favor to give me a good slippering for my

34
00:02:34,639 --> 00:02:39,197
misbehavior, anything indeed but condemning me to lie a bed such an

35
00:02:39,198 --> 00:02:44,078
endurable length of time. But she was the best and most conscientious of

36
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:49,038
stepmothers, and back I had to go to my room. For several hours I lay there

37
00:02:49,039 --> 00:02:53,278
broad awake, feeling a great deal worse than I have ever done since, even from

38
00:02:53,279 --> 00:02:56,078
the greatest subsequent misfortunes.

39
00:02:56,079 --> 00:03:01,438
At last I must have fallen into a troubled nightmare of a doze, and slowly

40
00:03:01,439 --> 00:03:07,038
waking from it, half steeped in dreams, I opened my eyes, and the before sunlit

41
00:03:07,039 --> 00:03:09,839
room was now wrapped in outer darkness.

42
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:14,638
Instantly I felt a shock running through all my frame. Nothing was to be seen and

43
00:03:14,639 --> 00:03:20,799
nothing was to be heard, but a supernatural hand seemed placed in mine.

44
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:26,157
My arm hung over the counterpane, and the nameless, unimaginable, silent form

45
00:03:26,158 --> 00:03:32,237
or phantom to which the hand belonged seemed closely seated by my bedside. For

46
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:37,599
what seemed ages piled on ages, I lay there frozen with the most awful fears,

47
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:42,559
not daring to drag away my hand. Yet, ever thinking that if I could but stir

48
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:47,839
at one single inch, the horrid spell would be broken. I knew not how this

49
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:52,157
consciousness at last glided away from me, but waking in the morning, I

50
00:03:52,158 --> 00:03:57,197
shudderingly remembered it all, and for days and weeks and months afterwards, I

51
00:03:57,198 --> 00:04:02,398
lost myself in confounding attempts to explain the mystery. Nay, to this very

52
00:04:02,399 --> 00:04:08,718
hour I often puzzle myself with it. Now take away the awful fear, and my

53
00:04:08,719 --> 00:04:13,519
sensations at feeling the supernatural hand in mine were very similar in their

54
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:18,799
stranges to those which I experienced on waking up and seeing Quequ's pagan arm

55
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:24,078
thrown around me. But at length all the past nights events soberly recurred one

56
00:04:24,079 --> 00:04:30,157
by one in fixed reality, and then I lay only alive to the comical predicament.

57
00:04:30,158 --> 00:04:35,118
For though I tried to move his arm, unlock his bridegroom clasp, yet

58
00:04:35,119 --> 00:04:39,197
sleeping as he was, he still hugged me tightly as though not but death should

59
00:04:39,198 --> 00:04:45,438
part us twain, I now strove to rouse him. Quiqu, but his only answer was a

60
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:50,638
snore. I then rolled over my neck, feeling as if it were in a horse collar,

61
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:53,278
and suddenly felt a slight scratch.

62
00:04:53,279 --> 00:04:56,959
Throwing aside the counterpane, there lay the tomahawk, sleeping by the

63
00:04:56,960 --> 00:05:01,759
savage's side, as if it were a hatchet-faced baby. A pretty pickle,

64
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:06,959
truly thought I, a bed here in a strange house in broad day with a cannibal and a

65
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:11,319
tomahawk. Quiquake.

66
00:05:13,119 --> 00:05:17,999
At length, by dent of much wriggling, and loud and incessant expostations upon

67
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:22,879
the unbecomingness of his hugging a fellow male in that matrimonial sort of

68
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:27,999
style, I succeeded in extracting a grunt, and presently he drew back his

69
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:32,318
arm, shook himself all over like a Newfoundland dog, just from the water,

70
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:36,718
and sat up in bed, stiff as a pike staff, looking at me and rubbing his

71
00:05:36,719 --> 00:05:41,038
eyes as if he did not altogether remember how I came to be there. though

72
00:05:41,039 --> 00:05:46,318
a dim consciousness of knowing something about me seemed slowly dawning over him.

73
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:51,599
Meanwhile I lay quietly eyeing him, having no serious misgivings now, and

74
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:57,278
bent upon narrowly observing so curious a creature. When at last his mind seemed

75
00:05:57,279 --> 00:06:01,118
made up, touching the character of his bedfellow, and he became, as it were,

76
00:06:01,119 --> 00:06:05,839
reconciled to the fact, he jumped out upon the floor, and by certain signs and

77
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:10,559
sounds, gave me to understand that, if it pleased me, he would dress first, and

78
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:15,358
then leave me to dress afterward, leaving the whole apartment to myself.

79
00:06:15,359 --> 00:06:19,678
Think I, Quiquake, under the circumstances, this is a very civilized

80
00:06:19,679 --> 00:06:23,999
overture. But the truth is, these savages have an innate sense of

81
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,398
delicacy. Say what you will. It is marvelous how essentially polite they

82
00:06:28,399 --> 00:06:33,438
are. I pay this particular compliment to Quiquake because he treated me with so

83
00:06:33,439 --> 00:06:38,478
much civility and consideration while I was guilty of great rudeness, staring at

84
00:06:38,479 --> 00:06:43,118
him from the bed and watching all of his twilelet motions. For the time my

85
00:06:43,119 --> 00:06:48,318
curiosity getting the better of my breeding. Nevertheless, a man likewig

86
00:06:48,319 --> 00:06:54,478
you don't see every day. He in his ways were well worth unusual regarding.

87
00:06:54,479 --> 00:06:59,999
He commenced dressing at top by dawning his beaver hat, a very tall one by the

88
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:05,759
by, and then, still, minus his trousers, he hunted up his boots. What under the

89
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,839
heavens he did it for, I cannot tell.

90
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:12,559
But his next movement was to crush himself, boots in hand, and hat on,

91
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:17,278
under the bed, when, from sundry, violent gaspings and strainings, I

92
00:07:17,279 --> 00:07:21,999
inferred he was hard at work booting himself, though by no law of propriety

93
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,759
that I ever heard of, is any man required to be private when putting on

94
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:30,959
his boots. But Quiquake, do you see was a creature in the transition stage,

95
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:35,919
neither caterpillar nor butterfly, he was just enough civilized to show off

96
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:40,799
his outlandishness in the strangest possible manners. His education was not

97
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:44,157
yet completed. He was an undergraduate.

98
00:07:44,158 --> 00:07:47,678
If he had not been a small degree civilized, he probably would not have

99
00:07:47,679 --> 00:07:52,478
troubled himself with boots at all. But then, if he had not been still a savage,

100
00:07:52,479 --> 00:07:57,038
he never would have dreamt of getting under the bed to put them on. At last he

101
00:07:57,039 --> 00:08:01,919
emerged with his hat very much dented and crushed down over his eyes and began

102
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:06,478
creaking and limping about the room as if not being much accustomed to boots.

103
00:08:06,479 --> 00:08:11,919
His pair of damp, wrinkled cowhide ones, probably not made to order either,

104
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:17,519
rather pinched and tormented him at the first go off of a bitter cold morning.

105
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:21,197
Seeing now that there were no curtains to the window, and that the street being

106
00:08:21,198 --> 00:08:25,759
very narrow, the house opposite commanded a plain view into the room,

107
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:29,839
and observing more and more the indecorous figure that Quiquake made,

108
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:34,318
staving about with little else but his hat and boots on, I begged him as well

109
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:38,879
as I could to accelerate his toilet somewhat, and particularly to get into

110
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:43,358
his pantaloons as soon as possible. He complied, and then proceeded to wash

111
00:08:43,359 --> 00:08:47,438
himself. At that time in the morning any Christian would have washed his face,

112
00:08:47,439 --> 00:08:51,999
but Quiquake, to my amazement, contented himself with restricting his ablutions

113
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:57,118
to his chest, arms, and hands. He then dawned his waist coat, and taking up a

114
00:08:57,119 --> 00:09:01,519
piece of hard soap on the wash stand center table, dipped it into water, and

115
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:06,718
commenced lathering his face. I was washing to see where he kept his razor,

116
00:09:06,719 --> 00:09:11,759
and lo and behold, he takes the harpoon from the bed corner, slips out the long

117
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:17,438
wooden stock, unshaths the head, wets it a little on his boot, and striding up to

118
00:09:17,439 --> 00:09:21,599
the bit of mirror against the wall, begins a vigorous scraping, or rather

119
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:26,559
harpooning of his cheeks. Thinks I quiquake, this is using Roger's best

120
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:31,358
cutlery with a vengeance. Afterwards, I wondered less at this operation when I

121
00:09:31,359 --> 00:09:36,078
came to know what fine steel the head of a harpoon is made, and how exceedingly

122
00:09:36,079 --> 00:09:39,999
sharp the long, straight edges are always kept.

123
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,999
The rest of his toilet was soon achieved, and he proudly marched out of

124
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,478
the room, wrapped up in his great pilot monkey jacket, and sporting his harpoon

125
00:09:48,479 --> 00:09:52,279
like a marshall's baton.
